You are building "Presnt" — an AI personal avatar app where a digital twin of the user looks like them, sounds like them, behaves like them, and acts on their behalf when they are unavailable.

PRODUCT VISION

The avatar:
- looks like the user
- sounds like the user
- behaves like the user
- acts on the user's behalf for delegated actions
- requests biometric approval for sensitive actions
- can be accessed by designated family members
- supports posthumous continuity settings

TECH STACK

- Flutter + Dart (iOS and Android)
- Claude API (behavioral model and response generation)
- ElevenLabs API (voice cloning and text to speech)
- HeyGen API (avatar face generation / preview integration)
- Firebase (Firestore, Authentication, Cloud Messaging)
- http package for API calls
- local biometric auth for Face ID / Touch ID approvals
- flutter_secure_storage for encrypted local secrets and sensitive local references

IMPORTANT ENGINEERING RULES

- Build the app with real Flutter code, not pseudocode
- Use mock data and placeholder integrations by default, but structure all services and models so real APIs can be plugged in later without changing UI architecture
- Do not hardcode secrets or API keys
- Do not log raw credential values, payment details, IDs, or other sensitive data
- Only masked credential values may appear in UI and logs
- Biometric approval must be required before sensitive credential access
- Use dark theme across the full app
- Keep code organized, readable, and ready to run
- Use a single consistent state management approach: Riverpod
- Use named routes or a clearly defined centralized navigation structure
- Add loading, empty, success, and error states to every important screen
- If a live API feature is not practical in the initial build, implement it as a clean placeholder flow with mock service responses

REAL VS PLACEHOLDER BEHAVIOR

For this build:
- Firebase Auth: real structure
- Firestore: real structure with mock/demo data support
- Claude: service wrapper + mock responses
- ElevenLabs: service wrapper + mock responses
- HeyGen: service wrapper + avatar preview placeholder
- Twilio / phone calling: placeholder only, not real calling yet
- Healthcare booking / email / external integrations: placeholder only
- Live conversations: simulated live session UI using mock transcript streaming, not actual phone infrastructure

